<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Finschhafen</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Finschhafen is a town on the Huon Peninsula in Morobe Province, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/papua-new-guinea">Papua New Guinea</a>. Founded in 1885 by the German <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-guinea">New Guinea</a> Company and named after the explorer Otto Finsch, it was the first capital of German New <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guinea">Guinea</a> until disease forced the administration to move in 1891. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a> it was the scene of heavy fighting in 1943.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/finschhafen.jpg" alt="Finschhafen" width="320" height="505" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: United States Bureau of Yards and Docks · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Finschhafen.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
